course: dictionary
lesson: 828
title: Beloved and the people we love
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Beloved means loved very much. «Our beloved family dog sleeps by the fire» tells you the family loves the dog a great deal. The word is like a hug: it is about love, and the more love, the more beloved.
explain: Context can show you how beloved is used. «A beloved children's author» means lots of children love this writer's books. The clue is the people who love the author, so beloved here means popular and dear to many readers.
explain: Beloved can also be a noun, a name for a person who is loved, especially a sweetheart. In «Aren't those beautiful words, Best Beloved?», Kipling is speaking to a listener he loves, so Best Beloved is a loving name for that person.
explain: You may hear «dearly beloved» at the start of a wedding. This is a church phrase for people who are dear to God or to each other. Dear and beloved are close in meaning, so you can swap one for the other to check.
fact: Beloved means loved very much.
fact: As a noun, a beloved is a person who is loved, especially a sweetheart. This use is old or poetic.
fact: «Dearly beloved» is a phrase often heard at the start of a wedding.
fact: Rudyard Kipling's Just So Stories (1902) begin with «O Best Beloved».
fact: A good check: swap in «loved very much» and see if the sentence still makes sense.
exercise: «The children's beloved teacher retired after thirty years.» What does beloved mean? | Hated by everyone | Lost and forgotten | *Loved very much | Very tired after work
exercise: At a wedding, the words «dearly beloved» are often heard. Where else might you hear this phrase? | In a science lab | At the supermarket checkout | In a football match | *In a church, at the start of a service
exercise: Kipling asks, «Aren't those beautiful words, Best Beloved?» In this sentence, what is Best Beloved? | A type of ship | *A person who is loved, the listener | A long word for a sentence | A chief of the Tribe
test: «Our beloved dog sleeps by the fire.» Which word is closest in meaning to beloved? | Empty | *Dear | Cold | Angry
test: «The Yellow Emperor is a beloved story.» What does beloved show here? | *Many people love the story | The story is wrong | The story is new | The story is very short
exam: Why is «Best Beloved» a loving name for the listener in Kipling's stories? | Because it is the name of a famous ship | Because it is a Chinese word | Because it means someone who is always late | *Because it means someone very dear, a person who is loved
